Arrays in DSA
An array is a data structure used to store multiple values of the same type in a single variable.
1. Simple Example
int mark1 = 80;
int mark2 = 75;
int mark3 = 90;
int mark4 = 85;

Traversing an Array
We can use a for loop to access every element.
for(int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    System.out.println(arr[i]);
}

Intializing in Array

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Declaration
        int[] arr;

        // Creating an array
        arr = new int[5];

        // Assigning values
        arr[0] = 10;
        arr[1] = 20;
        arr[2] = 30;
        arr[3] = 40;
        arr[4] = 50;

        // Printing the array
        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
            System.out.println(arr[i]);
        }
    }
}
